      "date": "2020-07-14",
      "status": "Final",
      "version": null,
      "parent_document_id": null,
      "version_group": null,
      "text": "STATEMENT OF DEFENCE\n\nMatter: Solanki Holdings v State Urban Development Authority\nMatter Code: DIS/BLR/0004/2020\nClient: Solanki Holdings Infra.\nAuthor: Ekavir Varkey (Associate)\nDate: 2020-07-14\nOffice: Bengaluru\n\nIN THE MATTER OF SOLANKI HOLDINGS V STATE URBAN DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY\nthe Tribunal\n\nRESPONDENT'S PLEADING\n\n1. The EPC Agreement governed the works / transaction.\n2. Material facts relied upon:\n   1. Delay caused by flooding / extreme rainfall\n3. The dispute turns on force majeure and related contractual machinery, including the treatment of exceptional weather event.\n4. Relief sought includes determination of liability and [amount to be inserted from quantum expert].\n5. The respondent will say: Flooding was foreseeable in monsoon geography; Contractor failed to mitigate; LD clause was a genuine pre-estimate.\n\nThis pleading is filed in DIS/BLR/0004/2020 without prejudice to amendment.\n",
